#       service: script.teach_face_dynamic

# ==============================================================================
# NOTES AND BEST PRACTICES
# ==============================================================================

# 1. TEACHING FACES:
#    - Use good lighting
#    - Face should be clearly visible and centered
#    - Only one person in frame
#    - Multiple angles can improve recognition (teach same person 2-3 times)

# 2. MATCHING:
#    - Confidence > 85% is generally reliable
#    - Confidence < 70% may be false positives
#    - Test with your specific cameras and lighting

# 3. PERFORMANCE:
#    - Face recognition is CPU intensive
#    - Don't scan too frequently (every 30-60 seconds is reasonable)
#    - Consider motion detection triggers instead of time-based

# 4. SECURITY:
#    - Face recognition should NOT be the only security measure
#    - Use it as convenience, not primary authentication
#    - Always have backup access methods

# 5. PRIVACY:
#    - Inform people they are being monitored
#    - Face encodings cannot be reversed to images
#    - All data stays local on your system

# ==============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ==============================================================================

# If services don't appear:
# 1. Check logs: /config/home-assistant.log
# 2. Verify folder structure: /config/custom_components/local_face_secure/
# 3. Restart Home Assistant twice

# If face recognition fails:
# 1. Check camera image quality
# 2. Ensure good lighting
# 3. Test with camera.front_door in Developer Tools
# 4. Check logs for specific errors

# If installation hangs:
# - face_recognition takes time to install (5-10 minutes)
# - Check system resources (needs ~1GB RAM for compilation)
# - Monitor logs during installation

# ==============================================================================
